{
  "description": "Golden fixtures (Paket 8, Phase B) for Filter and Remove, shared by the Rust engine (cargo test, src-tauri/src/text_processor.rs) and the JS engine (npm test, tests/unit/filter-remove.test.ts). They characterize the CURRENT behaviour: a passing test means the behaviour is described correctly, not that it is wanted. Every case states all options explicitly (no defaults). 'pattern' is a string or { repeat, count } (the string repeated count times). Filter expectations: the result text or { error: invalidRegex | regexRuntime }; JS only: { error: regexSplitsCharacter } (Paket 8 C1: a JS match would cut a surrogate pair apart, the worker refuses instead of returning damaged text). Remove expectations: { text, removedLines } or { error }. A case with different engine results uses expectedRust + expectedJs and a divergence { kind, reason }; kinds: dialect (accepted regex dialect difference, Paket 5), utf16Guard (Rust processes valid Unicode, JS refuses a result that would contain cut characters; required for regexSplitsCharacter), suspectedBug, inconsistentDefinition, unvalidatedInput. Every successful JS result must be well-formed Unicode. 'ref' points to the Phase A report (docs/analyse/Paket8-PhaseA-Filter-Remove-Analyse.md). 'openQuestion' marks identical behaviour that still needs a product decision. 'expectedJsUnreachableMainThread' characterizes FilterService.frontendInMainThread, which invoke never reaches (not a product path).",
